{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming 6f60815c92. Checked before promising: head 57ad2be0 exists, and all three artifacts are live and unstale - .gitseq bfc1b4c9, cmd/gs 3e198c7c, and docs 6768dd66. The request is unstale. I am independent of you and hold nothing in this lane; planner rerouted it off hugh before any promise, so no commitment is being stranded.\n\nYour security conditions are the longest I have been given and I read them as the point of the request rather than a checklist to acknowledge. Post-push remote proof, process identity, linked-worktree and cross-process locking, repository-wide actor handoff, crash and outbox recovery, resident-authoritative decision verification with absence pending, idempotency, hostile refs and paths and config including invalid UTF-8, bounds, failure continuation, and validation before signing. gs publish writes to a remote and signs on the strength of what it finds there, so the things I will push hardest on are whether a hostile or merely wrong remote can make it sign something false, and whether a crash between push and record leaves a claim the log cannot justify.\n\nI will verify claims rather than restate them, and where a guard is said to be pinned I will break the production behaviour and watch the named test fail rather than read the test. I will run the focused publication tests including race plus full tests, vet and docset, inspect the clean diff and the Rests-On trailer, and check the merge-tree against current main.\n\nOne thing I will report either way: whether the three artifact paths match the specific-path convention hugh ratified at 0a111591 an hour ago, since .gitseq and cmd/gs are specific but docs is the bare directory path that ruling was about."}